# pip-audit allowlist for Finlity
#
# Format:
#   - One CVE / GHSA / PYSEC ID per line.
#   - `#` lines are comments and are skipped.
#   - Blank lines are skipped.
#   - Each ID MUST be preceded by a `# reason: ...` comment on the line above.
#
# CI loads this file via scripts/ci-pip-audit.sh and turns each ID into a
# `--ignore-vuln <id>` argument to `pip-audit`. Any vuln NOT in this file
# fails the build. Keep this list as small as possible; prefer bumping the
# offending dependency in requirements.in (then re-pinning requirements.txt)
# over allowlisting.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-04-30 dependency-refresh sprint
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The 59-entry baseline was triaged by bumping direct deps in requirements.in
# (see commit history) and dropping `python-jose` (unused; removed entirely,
# which also dropped its transitive `ecdsa` and `pyasn1` CVEs). The four
# entries below are all transitive-only with no clean top-down fix yet, or
# require a major version bump that is out-of-scope for this sprint.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# reason: transitive via fastmcp; no upstream fix released for diskcache.
# fastmcp 2.x still depends on diskcache 5.6.3. Re-evaluate when fastmcp
# bumps the diskcache pin or when diskcache cuts a fixed release.
CVE-2025-69872

# reason: transitive via keyring (jsonschema dependency chain). Fix is in
# jaraco-context 6.1.0 but keyring 25.7.0 still constrains <= 6.0.x. Track
# upstream keyring release that loosens the pin.
CVE-2026-23949

# reason: transitive via fastmcp / rich. Fix is in pygments 2.20.0; drop
# this entry when fastmcp loosens its pygments pin (currently <2.20).
CVE-2026-4539

# reason: pytest 8.4.2 is the latest 8.x line. Fix is in 9.0.3, which is a
# major bump (collect/fixture API changes). Local-only DoS via predictable
# /tmp/pytest-of-{user} dirs — not exploitable in CI containers. Deferred
# to a follow-up "pytest 8 -> 9" migration ticket.
CVE-2025-71176

